Apple's stack probe, ___chkstk_darwin, as Xcode 27.0's clang calls it (B-170, docs/formats/build.md "Stack checks"),
written from Xcode's observed output (.github/scripts/clang_stack_experiments.py):
- the driver passes -fstack-check unasked to Apple devices from macOS 10.15, iOS and tvOS 13, watchOS 6, Mac Catalyst
  and visionOS, not to simulators, DriverKit, arm64_32 or -ffreestanding compiles; -fstack-check and -fno-stack-check
  are options instead of ignored flags;
- with it, every function of an Apple target gets "probe-stack"="__chkstk_darwin" ("___chkstk_darwin" on x86);
- AArch64: a frame of 4096 bytes of locals or more is probed after the callee saves, with its size in w9 and the probe
  called through x16 loaded from the GOT, with its linker optimization hint (lr kept around the call where the
  function does not save it, x9 to x12 where shrink-wrapping moved the prologue out of the entry block); a dynamic
  alloca calls it with the unrounded size in x9 (the size GlobalISel rounded at -O0), then takes the rounded size from
  sp; x9 to x11, x16, x17 and lr are not kept across the call;
- x86: every dynamic alloca calls the probe with the unrounded size, rounds it after the call and subtracts it; the
  call keeps the callee-saved and vector registers only; rax is pushed and popped around a prologue's call that the
  callee saves leave misaligned; leaf frames the probe does not need keep the red zone.
